# hplc-analyst — Project Plan

## Overview
A Python + FastAPI web application providing an AI-powered pharmaceutical HPLC analysis assistant, backed by the Claude API (Anthropic). The system prompt you provided will serve as the core persona for the LLM.

## Project Location
`/Users/paulbalas/Desktop/Projects/hplc-analyst`

## Tech Stack
- **Language:** Python 3.11+
- **Framework:** FastAPI (async, high-performance)
- **LLM:** Anthropic Claude API (claude-sonnet-4-20250514 default, claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 for fast tasks)
- **Frontend:** Minimal chat UI (HTML + Tailwind CSS + vanilla JS) — served by FastAPI's static files
- **Package Manager:** `uv` (fast Python package manager) with `pyproject.toml`
- **Environment:** `.env` for API keys (git-ignored)

## Project Structure
```
hplc-analyst/
├── app/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── main.py              # FastAPI app, CORS, static files, startup
│   ├── config.py            # Settings via pydantic-settings (.env loading)
│   ├── routers/
│   │   ├── __init__.py
│   │   └── chat.py          # POST /api/chat — streaming chat endpoint
│   ├── services/
│   │   ├── __init__.py
│   │   └── claude.py        # Anthropic SDK wrapper, system prompt loading
│   ├── prompts/
│   │   └── system.md        # The HPLC expert system prompt (your prompt text)
│   └── models/
│       ├── __init__.py
│       └── schemas.py       # Pydantic request/response models
├── static/
│   ├── index.html           # Chat UI
│   ├── app.js               # Chat logic (fetch + SSE streaming)
│   └── styles.css           # Minimal custom styles (Tailwind via CDN)
├── tests/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── test_chat.py         # API endpoint tests
│   └── test_claude.py       # Service layer tests
├── .env.example             # Template for env vars
├── .gitignore
├── pyproject.toml           # Dependencies + project metadata
└── README.md                # Setup & usage instructions
```

## Implementation Steps

### 1. Scaffold project directory & git init
- Initialize git repo
- Create `.gitignore` (Python standard + .env)

### 2. Create pyproject.toml with dependencies
- fastapi, uvicorn[standard], anthropic, pydantic-settings, python-dotenv
- Dev deps: pytest, httpx (for async test client)

### 3. Create app/config.py
- Pydantic Settings class loading from `.env`
- Keys: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `MODEL_NAME` (default: claude-sonnet-4-20250514), `MAX_TOKENS` (default: 8192)

### 4. Create app/prompts/system.md
- Store the full HPLC expert system prompt as a markdown file
- Loaded at startup by the service layer

### 5. Create app/services/claude.py
- Anthropic Python SDK client
- `chat()` async function: takes conversation history, returns streamed response
- System prompt injected automatically
- Retry logic with exponential backoff on rate limits (429)

### 6. Create app/models/schemas.py
- `ChatMessage` (role, content)
- `ChatRequest` (messages: list[ChatMessage], model: optional)
- `ChatResponse` (content, model, usage)

### 7. Create app/routers/chat.py
- `POST /api/chat` — accepts ChatRequest, returns streaming response (SSE)
- `GET /api/health` — health check

### 8. Create app/main.py
- FastAPI app with CORS middleware
- Mount static files at `/`
- Include chat router at `/api`

### 9. Create static/ chat UI
- Clean chat interface with Tailwind CSS
- Streaming response display (SSE)
- Conversation history maintained client-side
- Opening message from the system prompt

### 10. Create .env.example and .gitignore

### 11. Create basic tests
- Test health endpoint
- Test chat endpoint with mocked Claude response

### 12. Initial git commit
